   "versionNonce": 479402029,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1762600000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "INTRODUCTION",
   "originalText": "INTRODUCTION",
   "fontSize": 28,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseline": 25
  },
  {
   "id": "tex10_2013",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 80,
   "y": 275,
   "width": 1116.0,
   "height": 25.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1239319144,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1257440635,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1762600000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "These notes cover how backend full-stack development and agentic AI work together in 2026.",
   "originalText": "These notes cover how backend full-stack development and agentic AI work together in 2026.",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseline": 18
  },
  {
   "id": "tex11_7499",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 80,
   "y": 322.0,
   "width": 1537.6,
   "height": 100.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 106492239,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 2096491879,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1762600000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "BACKEND FULL-STACK DEVELOPMENT is the part of an app that runs on the server. It receives requests from the frontend, checks\nwho the user is, applies the business rules, reads and writes data in a database, and sends back a response. Today this is\nusually built with TypeScript (Node.js, Next.js) or Python (FastAPI), with Postgres as the database. Login, payments and\nhosting are mostly handled by ready services like Clerk, Stripe or Razorpay, Supabase and Vercel.",
   "originalText": "BACKEND FULL-STACK DEVELOPMENT is the part of an app that runs on the server. It receives requests from the frontend, checks\nwho the user is, applies the business rules, reads and writes data in a database, and sends back a response. Today this is\nusually built with TypeScript (Node.js, Next.js) or Python (FastAPI), with Postgres as the database. Login, payments and\nhosting are mostly handled by ready services like Clerk, Stripe or Razorpay, Supabase and Vercel.",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseline": 18
  },
  {
   "id": "tex12_4622",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 80,
   "y": 444.0,
   "width": 1550.0,
   "height": 100.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 100035545,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1195428768,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1762600000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "AGENTIC AI means an AI model that does not just answer a question but works toward a goal. It runs in a loop: it plans a\nstep, calls a tool (an API, a database, a browser), looks at the result, and decides what to do next. It stops when the task\nis done. Agents use memory to remember past steps, RAG to look up the right information, and protocols like MCP to connect to\ntools in a standard way.",
   "originalText": "AGENTIC AI means an AI model that does not just answer a question but works toward a goal. It runs in a loop: it plans a\nstep, calls a tool (an API, a database, a browser), looks at the result, and decides what to do next. It stops when the task\nis done. Agents use memory to remember past steps, RAG to look up the right information, and protocols like MCP to connect to\ntools in a standard way.",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseline": 18
  },
  {
   "id": "tex13_3181",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 80,
   "y": 566.0,
   "width": 1550.0,
   "height": 75.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 621931212,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 900094242,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1762600000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The two fields now meet in one place: THE BACKEND IS WHERE AGENTS LIVE. The backend gives the agent its tools, stores its\nmemory and state, streams its answers to the user, keeps long tasks running, and adds safety checks such as rate limits, logs\nand human approval before risky actions.",
   "originalText": "The two fields now meet in one place: THE BACKEND IS WHERE AGENTS LIVE. The backend gives the agent its tools, stores its\nmemory and state, streams its answers to the user, keeps long tasks running, and adds safety checks such as rate limits, logs\nand human approval before risky actions.",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseline": 18
  },
  {
   "id": "tex14_3363",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 80,
   "y": 663.0,
   "width": 1537.6,
   "height": 50.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1161114103,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 252956897,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1762600000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "These notes go through both sides step by step: first the core backend building blocks, then how AI agents are designed, and\nfinally how to put them together into a real, reliable product.",
   "originalText": "These notes go through both sides step by step: first the core backend building blocks, then how AI agents are designed, and\nfinally how to put them together into a real, reliable product.",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseline": 18
  },
  {
   "id": "rec15_6054",
